menu "Bicopter sensor hardware"

    config BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        bool "Physical IMU/barometer sensors are wired to this board"
        default n
        help
            No ESP32 board/pinout has been finalized for this project yet (see docs/hardware.md).
            Leave disabled until a board is chosen and the I2C pins below are set to match it -
            SensorTask (firmware/main/sensor_task.c) gracefully skips real sensor I2C init/reads
            while this is disabled, logging a stub reading instead of attempting a bus that
            doesn't exist. Flip this on and fill in the pins below once a board with an MPU6050
            and BMP581 wired up exists.

    config BICOPTER_I2C_PORT
        int "I2C port number"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 0

    config BICOPTER_I2C_SDA_GPIO
        int "I2C SDA GPIO"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 21
        help
            Placeholder default (ESP32's commonly-used default I2C SDA pin) - not verified against
            any actual board wiring. Set to match the real board once one is chosen.

    config BICOPTER_I2C_SCL_GPIO
        int "I2C SCL GPIO"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 22
        help
            Placeholder default (ESP32's commonly-used default I2C SCL pin) - not verified against
            any actual board wiring. Set to match the real board once one is chosen.

    config BICOPTER_I2C_CLOCK_HZ
        int "I2C clock speed (Hz)"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 400000
        help
            400kHz ("fast mode") - both the MPU6050 and BMP581 support it per their datasheets.

    config BICOPTER_MPU6050_INT_GPIO
        int "MPU6050 data-ready interrupt GPIO (-1 disables, falls back to polling)"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default -1
        help
            See firmware/components/sensors/include/mpu6050.h - GPIO_NUM_NC (-1) makes
            mpu6050_read() poll the INT_STATUS data-ready bit each call instead of blocking on an
            interrupt-fed queue. Set to a real GPIO once the MPU6050's INT pin is wired to one.

endmenu

menu "Bicopter radio (ESP-NOW)"

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        bool "ESP-NOW radio link is paired with a ground-station peer"
        default n
        help
            No ground-station peer has been paired or tested in this environment yet (no physical
            hardware - see docs/radio.md). Leave disabled until a peer MAC is configured below and
            two real ESP32 boards are available to pair. RadioTask (firmware/main/radio_task.c)
            gracefully skips Wi-Fi/ESP-NOW init while this is disabled, logging a stub cadence
            instead of bringing up a radio link that has nothing to talk to.

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_PEER_MAC
        string "Paired peer MAC address (AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF)"
        depends on BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        default "FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF"
        help
            Placeholder broadcast address - replace with the ground-station peer's real MAC once
            one is chosen and paired. See docs/radio.md's pairing procedure.

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "Wi-Fi channel"
        depends on BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 1
        help
            Both peers must be set to the same fixed channel - ESP-NOW rides on the Wi-Fi radio
            without an actual AP association/channel negotiation. Valid range 1-13
            (region-dependent).

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Command staleness timeout (ms)"
        depends on BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 500
        help
            has_command()/get_health().link_alive (firmware/components/radio/include/radio.h)
            report the link lost if no valid command packet is received within this window. 500ms
            is a placeholder, 10x RadioTask's own 20ms/50Hz cycle - see docs/radio.md. The actual
            failsafe *behavior* once the link is considered lost is Milestone 16's job, not this
            option's.

endmenu
